{"author":{"id":"1e0a6ff3e01313072cf7b3803c158c22d01a37717237fe198e814e781752b172"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1785786061,"nonce":"jmtpN6MyDa/ERgFl9/ShxHRKqPM=","message":"Experiment results: the scissors approach proposed at the end of the\nthread (posting the patch under \"-- \u003e8 --\" in a plain reply) does NOT\nwork with current b4.\n\nSetup: offline mboxes with (A) a plain bug-report message plus a reply\ncarrying a fix under scissors, and (B) the shazam-git1-just-series\n4-patch sample series plus the same kind of scissors reply to the\ncover. Retrieval via \"b4 --offline-mode am -C -m \u003cmbox\u003e -o-\", with a\ncontrol run without the scissors reply.\n\nFindings:\n\n1. The scissors patch cannot be retrieved at all. \"b4 am \u003creply-msgid\u003e\"\n   on the bug-report thread reports \"No patches found\"; on the series\n   thread it silently resolves to the parent series instead. Even\n   --single-message on the reply gives \"No patches found\". Thread\n   analysis classifies patches by subject (\"Re: ...\" is a follow-up,\n   never a patch); the scissors handling in\n   LoreMessage.get_am_message() (src/b4/__init__.py:3301) only runs\n   after a message is already classified as a patch, so the diff below\n   the scissors is never considered.\n\n2. The parent series is not hijacked: retrieving the cover with the\n   scissors reply in-thread still yields exactly the original 4\n   patches. This is better than the direct-reply-patch pattern that\n   started the thread.\n\n3. Trailer pollution: with the scissors reply in the thread, all four\n   parent patches acquired the Signed-off-by from inside the scissors\n   patch. Trailers embedded in the under-scissors patch (SOB,\n   Reported-by, etc.) are harvested as follow-up trailers and applied\n   to the entire parent series. Confirmed against the control run.\n\nConclusion: making this workflow viable would require scissors\nawareness in thread analysis: (a) recognize a \"Re:\" message containing\nan under-scissors patch as a standalone patch retrievable via its own\nmsgid, and (b) exclude below-scissors content from follow-up trailer\nmining.","files":null}]}